=== Gap-fill evidence for Scenario 3 (component-traceability v2.0, sequence 2) ===
Generated to replace two illustrative, unverified claims previously written in
the dissertation's Scenario 3 text ("component COMP-1001 is already
registered" and a 92C WARRANTY_VOID result), neither of which actually
appeared in any of this repository's other evidence/*.log files. This log
supplies the same two outcomes as real, unedited peer chaincode invoke/query
output against the live network.

  1. RegisterComponent duplicate-ID rejection: a second RegisterComponent
     call using an identifier already on the ledger (COMP-DUP-1) is rejected.
  2. WarrantyCheck: a component is taken through the full lifecycle to
     DELIVERED, given a RecordUsageLog reading of 92C, and WarrantyCheck
     against an 85C threshold returns WARRANTY_VOID with fault USER, with an
     explicit wait after every state-changing call so the query reads
     post-commit state (the same commit-timing lesson documented in
     real_fabric_run1_timing_lesson.log / real_fabric_run2_full_scenario.log).
